        "original_id": "2c8f4956-9f0c-537c-9d7f-68b59c1e8433",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Iowa, University of Texas at Austin\n- Places: Iowa City, Iowa, Austin, Texas, Texas State Capitol, Chicago\n- People: David Loughery\n- Programs: Iowa Playwrights Workshop\n- Concepts: public research universities, colleges, areas of study, professional degrees\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Iowa was founded in 1847 and is the oldest university in the state of Iowa.\n- The University of Texas at Austin was founded in 1881 as \"The University of Texas.\"\n- The University of Iowa is a flagship public research university in Iowa City, Iowa, and it is also known as the UI, U of I, UIowa, and Iowa.\n- The University of Iowa is organized into eleven colleges that offer more than 200 areas of study and seven professional degrees.\n- The University of Texas at Austin campus is located in Austin, Texas, about 1 mile from the Texas State Capitol.\n- David Loughery was born in Chicago and attended Ball State University and the University of Iowa.\n- David Loughery was a member of the Iowa Playwrights Workshop at the University of Iowa.",
